# WM_SETCURSOR in the client area
ok handled: result 1
ok graphic child under the mouse: its cursor
ok no child under the mouse: the window control's cursor
ok crDefault child: the parent's cursor
ok disabled graphic child: not under the mouse
ok crDefault up the whole chain: arrow
ok crNone: no cursor
# UIF-021 mapping
ok crIBeam
ok crHourGlass
ok crHSplit
ok crNoDrop
ok crDrag
# non-client hit codes
ok HTCAPTION: default processing
# Screen.Cursor
ok default crDefault
ok applied at once
ok wins over the control's cursor
ok reset: the control's cursor again
# CM_CURSORCHANGED
ok the control under the mouse: applied at once
ok another control: nothing happens
ok back to crDefault: the inherited cursor
